-- title:
--   Krull dimension one for the special fibre of the j-finite Igusa chart
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a natural number with $N \neq 0$ and let $\ell$ be a prime. Write $\Lambda = \mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$, and let $F$ denote the field `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, in which `jFull N` is the element $j$. Let $A =$ `chartAlgFin N ℓ` be the $\Lambda$-subalgebra of $F$ whose elements are those $x \in F$ integral over the $\Lambda$-subalgebra generated by $j$, that is, the integral closure of $\Lambda[j]$ in $F$. Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $\ell$ equipped with a $\Lambda$-algebra structure, and let $\mathfrak{m}$ be a maximal ideal of the tensor product $k \otimes_{\Lambda} A$. Then the localisation of $k \otimes_{\Lambda} A$ at $\mathfrak{m}$ has Krull dimension equal to $1$ (as an element of $\mathbb{N}_{\infty}$, hence in particular finite and non-zero). No assumption relating $\ell$ to $N$, and no assumption that $k$ be algebraically closed, is made.
--
--   This is the dimension half of the ring-theoretic form of Igusa's theorem on the special fibre of the $j$-finite chart of the Igusa model: the fibre over a characteristic-$\ell$ point of the normal model finite over the $j$-line is equidimensional of dimension one. It is used by [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.isRegularLocalRing_localization_chartAlgFin_tensor`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.isRegularLocalRing_localization_chartAlgFin_tensor), and, through that, in the flatness and fibre-dimension statements [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.flat_pi`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.flat_pi) and [`ModularCurve.DRLevel.not_isOpen_singleton_fibre`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRLevel.not_isOpen_singleton_fibre).
